{
  "_readme": "Nono & Fofo Adventure (Mario-style challenge). Each level is a text map: one string per row, top row first, every row the same length; 1 character = 1 tile. Legend: '.' air, 'G' ground, 'S' stone block, 'B' brick (big Nono breaks it), '?' coin block, 'L' letter block (exactly 'letters' of them, in order), 'P' Grandpa's page block (grow into Nono), 'o' coin, '@' start, 'K' checkpoint flag, 'E' the letters gate (Grandpa's book is just after it), 'd' duck, 's' scorpion, 'c' crab, 'g' seagull, 'm' platform moving sideways (3 tiles), 'v' platform moving up and down (3 tiles), 'f' falling tile, 'h' hidden coin block (invisible until bumped from below, gives 6 coins), 'X' a place the bonus letter may hide (one X is picked at random each play; finding it adds 2 stars). A column with no ground at the bottom is a hole. Physics numbers are in tiles and seconds. Stars: finish = 1, coins >= stars[0] of the level's coins = 2, >= stars[1] = 3.",
